{"unit_slug":"monk_focus_points","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","scale_numeric_bonus","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","modifies","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"shared_resource_pool","justification":"Focus Points is a pool of N points shared across multiple distinct sub-features. The current UseCountResource models per-feature use counts, not a shared expendable pool. This requires either a new resource kind (e.g. FocusPool with a cap and a per-use cost) or a new ClassFeatureMechanics family that separates pool definition from pool-consumer sub-features.","evidence":"You can expend these points to enhance or fuel certain Monk features. You start knowing three such features: Flurry of Blows, Patient Defense, and Step of the Wind."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"multi_sub_feature_activation","justification":"ClassFeatureActivationMechanics supports exactly one effect. Focus Points has three distinct named sub-activations (Flurry of Blows, Patient Defense, Step of the Wind), each with its own cost and effect. There is no way to express a feature with multiple named sub-activations in the current family.","evidence":"You start knowing three such features: Flurry of Blows, Patient Defense, and Step of the Wind, each of which is detailed below."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"dual_mode_activation","justification":"Patient Defense and Step of the Wind each have a free baseline mode (no focus point cost, just a Bonus Action) AND an enhanced mode (costs 1 Focus Point for a combined effect). There is no variant in ClassFeatureActivationCost or ClassFeatureEffect that models 'free baseline OR enhanced by spending a resource point'.","evidence":"Patient Defense: You can take the Disengage action as a Bonus Action. Alternatively, you can expend 1 Focus Point to take both the Disengage and the Dodge actions as a Bonus Action."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_unarmed_strikes","justification":"Flurry of Blows grants two Unarmed Strikes as a Bonus Action. This is distinct from grant_extra_action (which grants one extra action from the standard action menu). Two unarmed strikes are not an Attack action — they are specific attack instances with the Unarmed Strike weapon type. No current atom captures 'grant N Unarmed Strikes'.","evidence":"Flurry of Blows. You can expend 1 Focus Point to make two Unarmed Strikes as a Bonus Action."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"double_jump_distance","justification":"Step of the Wind (enhanced mode) doubles the character's jump distance for the turn. This is a movement-modifier effect with no existing atom. The current effect vocabulary (damage, heal, grant_extra_action, modify_ac, etc.) contains nothing for jump/movement distance scaling.","evidence":"Step of the Wind: ...you can expend 1 Focus Point to take both the Disengage and Dash actions as a Bonus Action, and your jump distance is doubled for the turn."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"take_standard_action_as_bonus","justification":"Patient Defense (free mode) and Step of the Wind (free mode) allow the monk to take a standard action (Disengage / Dash) as a Bonus Action. This is not grant_extra_action — it converts an existing standard action into a Bonus Action usage. The current grant_extra_action atom grants an additional action from the action menu, not a standard-action-to-bonus-action substitution. A new atom is needed to express 'may use action X as a Bonus Action'.","evidence":"Patient Defense. You can take the Disengage action as a Bonus Action. / Step of the Wind. You can take the Dash action as a Bonus Action."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"class_feature_save_dc","justification":"The feature specifies a save DC computed as 8 + Wisdom modifier + Proficiency Bonus, used by features that consume Focus Points. This is distinct from caster_spell_save_dc (which is tied to the spellcasting system and uses the spellcasting ability). DcSource needs a new variant that specifies the ability (wis here) and the formula base (8 + ability mod + PB) as a class feature DC.","evidence":"Some features that use Focus Points require your target to make a saving throw. The save DC equals 8 plus your Wisdom modifier and Proficiency Bonus."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.29}
