{"unit_slug":"rogue_sneak_attack","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"damage_on_hit (class_feature effect)","justification":"Sneak Attack's core payload is bonus weapon-type damage on a successful attack hit, conditioned on advantage-or-ally. ClassFeatureEffect only has grant_extra_action and heal_hp. Neither expresses conditional on-hit damage. The spell surface has DamageOnHitOperation inside ongoing_effect, but that is spell-family-only. A parallel effect atom for class features is required.","evidence":"you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack roll"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"activation_condition (class_feature conditional trigger predicate)","justification":"Sneak Attack fires only when a disjunctive condition holds: (Advantage on the roll) OR (ally within 5 ft of target, ally not Incapacitated, and no Disadvantage). No conditional trigger grammar exists anywhere in ClassFeatureMechanics. A new predicate atom is needed to express advantage-state checks and ally-proximity checks.","evidence":"if you have Advantage on the roll ... You don't need Advantage on the attack roll if at least one of your allies is within 5 feet of the target, the ally doesn't have the Incapacitated condition, and you don't have Disadvantage on the attack roll."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"weapon_category_filter (finesse | ranged)","justification":"Sneak Attack is restricted to attacks made with a Finesse or Ranged weapon. No weapon-category filter atom exists for class features (or at all in the surface). Without this, the surface cannot distinguish Sneak Attack from a generic damage bonus.","evidence":"the attack uses a Finesse or a Ranged weapon"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"DamageType: weapon_type (weapon-relative source)","justification":"The extra damage type is 'the same as the weapon's type', which is a runtime-resolved value determined by the equipped weapon, not a fixed physical damage type. The current DamageType is a closed enum of 13 specific types (acid, bludgeoning, … slashing). A new variant (or a separate DamageTypeSource discriminant) is needed to express weapon-relative damage.","evidence":"The extra damage's type is the same as the weapon's type."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"RestResetCadence: once_per_turn","justification":"Sneak Attack resets its once-per-use limit each turn, not on a rest. RestResetCadence has no turn variant — only short_or_long_rest, long_rest, short_rest, partial_short_full_long. Without this, the resource gate cannot be correctly modeled.","evidence":"Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"ClassFeatureMechanics: on_hit_conditional family","justification":"Taken together, the required atoms (conditional trigger, weapon-category filter, once-per-turn gate, weapon-relative damage-on-hit with class-level scaling) compose a new structural family that is not a variant of ClassFeatureActivationMechanics. It is analogous to mastery's on_hit_trigger family but for class features with conditional predicates and level scaling. A new ClassFeatureMechanics union member is the appropriate architecture.","evidence":"Once per turn … if you have Advantage … or ally within 5 feet … Finesse or Ranged weapon … extra 1d6 … The extra damage increases as you gain Rogue levels"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'heal' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'scale_die_count' not in tracer output","tracer emitted atom 'grant_extra_action' not in claude's claim"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.291}
{"unit_slug":"barbarian_rage","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"ClassFeatureEffect.ongoing_state","justification":"Rage's effect is a persistent state with multiple simultaneous sub-effects, a max duration (10 min), early-termination conditions, and a turn-by-turn renewal mechanic. None of the existing ClassFeatureEffect variants (grant_extra_action, heal_hp) model this. This is the root atom_widening — the tracer throws 'unhandled class-feature effect' on the 'ongoing_state' kind.","evidence":"While active, your Rage follows the rules below. [...] The Rage lasts until the end of your next turn, and it ends early if you don Heavy armor or have the Incapacitated condition."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"damage_resistance","justification":"Rage grants resistance to three damage types (BPS) while active. No damage_resistance atom exists anywhere in ClassFeatureEffect. The closest analog in spells is Stoneskin's mechanics, but class features have no resistance effect type.","evidence":"Damage Resistance. You have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"bonus_damage","justification":"Rage adds a flat bonus (+2/+3/+4 by class level) to damage rolls for Strength weapon attacks and Unarmed Strikes. No bonus_damage class-feature effect atom exists. This is a damage rider conditioned on the attack using Strength, scaling by class level via threshold_tiers.","evidence":"Rage Damage. When you make an attack using Strength — with either a weapon or an Unarmed Strike — and deal damage to the target, you gain a bonus to the damage that increases as you gain levels as a Barbarian."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"advantage_on_ability","justification":"Rage grants Advantage on Strength ability checks AND Strength saving throws. No advantage_on_ability class-feature effect atom exists. The mastery surface has modify_roll_advantage but that is a on-hit rider, not an ongoing state effect on the activating creature.","evidence":"Strength Advantage. You have Advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"disable_actions","justification":"Rage prohibits maintaining Concentration and casting spells. No disable_actions atom exists. This is a constraint on the Raging creature's available action types while the state is active.","evidence":"No Concentration or Spells. You can't maintain Concentration, and you can't cast spells."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"early_termination_condition","justification":"Rage ends early on two conditions: donning Heavy armor or gaining the Incapacitated condition. These are state-watch predicates on the activating creature. No early_termination_condition atom or lifecycle variant handles this pattern.","evidence":"it ends early if you don Heavy armor or have the Incapacitated condition"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"turn_renewal","justification":"Rage's duration lasts until end of next turn but can be extended each turn by one of: making an attack roll against an enemy, forcing an enemy to make a saving throw, or taking a Bonus Action. This renewal-on-action pattern is entirely absent from the current duration/lifecycle vocabulary (only instantaneous, concentration, timed persist/expire exist).","evidence":"If your Rage is still active on your next turn, you can extend the Rage for another round by doing one of the following: Make an attack roll against an enemy. Force an enemy to make a saving throw. Take a Bonus Action to extend your Rage."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"UseCountCap.unlimited","justification":"Level 17+ Barbarian has unlimited Rage uses per day. UseCountCap = { kind: 'fixed' } | ThresholdTiers<number> — neither can express 'unlimited'. A new { kind: 'unlimited' } variant is needed.","evidence":"Level 17 row of the Barbarian Features table shows 'Unlimited' in the Rages column."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'bonus_action_quota' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'scale_numeric_bonus' not in tracer output","tracer emitted atom 'grant_extra_action' not in claude's claim"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.35}
{"unit_slug":"paladin_lay_on_hands","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"hp_pool","justification":"Lay On Hands uses a replenishable numeric HP point pool (capacity = 5 × paladin level) that is drawn down by variable amounts across multiple uses per rest cycle. UseCountResource models discrete use-counts decremented by 1 per activation; it cannot represent a pool where each activation depletes an arbitrary number of HP (1 to pool_remaining). The pool is shared across both uses (heal HP and cure condition), so the resource atom must support partial draws, not just fixed-use-count decrement.","evidence":"you have a pool of healing power that replenishes when you finish a Long Rest. With that pool, you can restore a total number of Hit Points equal to five times your Paladin level"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"remove_condition (ClassFeatureEffect variant)","justification":"The secondary use expends 5 HP from the pool to remove the Poisoned condition without restoring HP. ClassFeatureEffect only has heal_hp and grant_extra_action; neither represents condition removal. A remove_condition variant requires at minimum a condition name (Condition) and a pool cost (number of HP spent), and must be expressible as an alternative to heal_hp that draws from the same hp_pool.","evidence":"You can also expend 5 Hit Points from the pool of healing power to remove the Poisoned condition from the creature; those points don't also restore Hit Points to the creature."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"variable_draw (DiceAmount variant)","justification":"The heal amount is 'up to the maximum amount remaining in the pool' — a player-chosen integer between 1 and pool_remaining at activation time. DiceAmount offers fixed, threshold_tiers, and linear_per_level — all compute a determined amount. None express a bounded player choice. This variant would need a reference to the hp_pool atom and a draw semantic (e.g., draw: 'up_to_pool_remaining').","evidence":"you can touch a creature (which could be yourself) and draw power from the pool of healing to restore a number of Hit Points to that creature, up to the maximum amount remaining in the pool"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"dual_use_pool_draw","justification":"Lay On Hands presents two mutually-exclusive activation modes (heal HP vs. cure Poisoned condition) both drawing from a single shared hp_pool. ClassFeatureActivationMechanics has a single effect field with no branching or choice mechanism. A dual-use subgraph needs: (1) a choice node (player selects heal or cure), (2) each branch specifying a pool draw cost and effect, (3) the shared hp_pool resource consumed by whichever branch fires.","evidence":"you can touch a creature … and draw power from the pool … [to heal] … You can also expend 5 Hit Points from the pool … to remove the Poisoned condition"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'bonus_action_quota' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'heal' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'scale_numeric_bonus' not in tracer output","tracer emitted atom 'grant_extra_action' not in claude's claim"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.465}
